course: dictionary
lesson: 15734
title: Words that spread
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Transmissible is a long word, but you can break it into parts. Transmit means to pass something on, and -ible means able to be. So transmissible means able to be passed on from one person to another.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Measles is very transmissible, so sick children should stay at home.» The sentence is about illness and staying away from others, so the word must be about spreading. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Measles is very able to be passed on" is clumsy, but the idea fits.
explain: Look for the phrases around the word. «A highly transmissible disease» means it spreads very easily. «More transmissible» compares two things: one spreads more easily than the other. Highly and more tell you how strong the spreading is.
fact: Transmissible means able to be passed from one person, animal or thing to another.
fact: Transmissible is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a disease.
fact: In science and health lessons, transmissible diseases are linked to germs, infections and vaccines.
fact: Washing hands and covering coughs can reduce how many people catch a transmissible disease.
fact: In a more formal use, traits passed from parents to children can also be called transmissible.
exercise: «Measles is very transmissible.» What does transmissible mean? | *Able to be passed from one person to another | Very tasty and sweet | Kept safely in a box | Impossible to see with the eye
exercise: «The doctor said the flu was highly transmissible.» What does highly transmissible mean? | Good for your heart | Very rare and never seen before | Hard to pronounce | *Spreads very easily from person to person
exercise: Which action helps reduce how many people catch a transmissible disease? | Eating sweets all day | Sharing a cup and a towel with friends | *Washing hands and covering coughs | Staying up very late
test: «Which word fits? The virus was so ___ that it spread across the whole school in a week.» | Luminous | Fragile | Curt | *Transmissible
test: «Vaccines help stop a disease that is ___ from one person to another.» | *Transmissible | Ancient | Drooped | Barely
exam: In «a transmissible trait passed from parents to children», what could transmissible mean? | Painted in bright colours | *Able to be passed on to the next generation | Very sad and heartbroken | Hidden under a bed
